{
    "test_name": "MOB.356_Work_Charge_Form_Validity",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.356_Work_Charge_Form_Validity",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.356` **Trap 8 across all four charge forms** \u2014 the negative case `MOB.350`\u2013`MOB.380`\nnever covered.\n- **The gap**: those four each add a charge with *valid* input. Four happy paths. None\n  proves what an INVALID form does \u2014 and `SubmitButton.tsx:14` is\n  `type={isValid ? 'submit' : 'button'}`, so pressing an invalid Submit does **nothing**:\n  no error, no toast. *\"Clicked, no toast\"* is indistinguishable from *\"worked, toast\n  missed\"*, which is what once cost `MOB.380` several runs of misdiagnosis.\n- **One test, four forms \u2014 because they are ONE component.** All four render through\n  `WorkCollectionForm` (`ui/Form.tsx:80`), emitting a single `<form\n  id=\"work-collection-form\">`. Four separate tests would cover no extra branch.\n- \u2b50 **Proven two independent ways.** `SubmitButton` expresses invalidity twice \u2014 the\n  `type` attribute (semantics) and `opacity: 0.5` (appearance, read via\n  `getComputedStyle`, the `MOB.342` technique). The attribute alone would pass on a\n  mislabelled button; the opacity alone on any dimmed element. Together they pin\n  `isValid`.\n- \u26a0\ufe0f **Only the ADD (CREATE) form is opened.** Validity differs by mode: CREATE is\n  `isValid`, UPDATE is `isValid && isDirty` \u2014 so an inert Submit on an *existing* charge\n  would prove **dirtiness**, not validity. A future UPDATE leg must assert something\n  different and say so.\n- \ud83d\uded1 **Strictly read-only**: nothing typed, nothing submitted, every form escaped. Safe\n  beside the four write tests in a shared session, and it cannot eat fixture data.",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Work Orders",
            "read-only"
        ],
